{"changes":["eka-core/scripts/coverage.floor: a floor per package. A module-wide total is dominated by whichever package has the most statements, so a collapse in a small high-risk package vanishes inside it; comparing each package against its own floor is what makes that collapse visible.","eka-core/scripts/coverage-gate.sh: runs the suite once with the existing race configuration and coverage, prints a per-package table, and fails when a package is below its floor or has no floor at all — a new package must declare one rather than slipping in unmeasured.","eka-core/.github/workflows/ci.yml: the test step is now the gate, so coverage is enforced on the run that already happened rather than an extra one.","eka-core/metadata/capture_test.go (7 tests): the ADR-035 v3 defaults, a fully-set capture block, a partial block that must keep the defaults for the fields it omits, the dedupeWindow grammar through both parseDedupeWindow and Parse, the closed provenance filter set, and Marshal's round-trip and fixed-point behaviour including that an absent field is not rendered as a zero value.","eka-core/runtime/dedupe_test.go (9 tests): Similarity's identical, empty and normalization cases; short-title singular/plural deduping through the Levenshtein fallback; unrelated titles staying apart; symmetry and the [0,1] bound; levenshteinRatio's edges; ContextBudget's priority ordering and truncation guard; DeltaCache's two not-modified paths and its stale-version negative case; the dedupe window boundaries."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Covered the capture dedupe path and metadata's configuration surface, and replaced one module-wide coverage number with a per-package gate.","tests":["metadata 47.3% -\u003e 95.6%, runtime 62.7% -\u003e 65.3%, measured with -race through the new gate.","coverage-gate.sh run end to end: prints the 13-package table and reports ok; the sed extraction and the below-floor comparison were checked separately against sample output.","go test ./... -count=1 in eka-core -\u003e all packages ok. go build ./... , go vet ./... , gofmt -l . -\u003e clean.","The new runtime tests found two behaviours that are now recorded rather than silently changed: Similarity's Levenshtein fallback does not cover the three-token example its own comment cites (filed as bug:capture-dedupe-fallback-narrow), and Similarity(\"\",\"\") is 1.0, safe only because DedupeCheckByTitle refuses an empty title first."]}